 "result": "The failing call is in `src/tessel/sessions.py`, in `SignedCookieSessionInterface.persist_session`. The traceback points at line 374, the `response.set_cookie(` call:\n\n```python\nresponse.set_cookie(\n    name,\n    val,\n    expires=expires,\n    httponly=httponly,\n    domain=domain,\n    path=path,\n    secure=secure,\n    partitioned=partitioned,\n    samesite=samesite,\n)\n```\n\nThe rejected argument is **`partitioned=partitioned`**. Werkzeug 3.0.3 raises `TypeError: Response.set_cookie() got an unexpected keyword argument 'partitioned'`.\n\nThe same keyword is also passed to `response.delete_cookie(...)` earlier in that function, in the branch that clears an empty modified session. No test I saw reached that branch, so I don't know whether it fails the same way.",
